WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:01.229
All right.

00:00:01.229 --> 00:00:06.470
We've got some very sick and needy audience
questions today, some of which are coming

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:08.080
right at me and I love it.

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:09.099
Let's get to the first one.

00:00:09.099 --> 00:00:16.160
David, aren't you a hypocrite for criticizing
our financial system and then making money

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:19.589
from it, investing in stocks and bonds?

00:00:19.589 --> 00:00:25.050
And I'm sure paying as little in taxes as
you are legally allowed to.

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:28.449
No, no, I am not a hypocrite.

00:00:28.449 --> 00:00:29.630
Listen.

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:33.010
This has been explored in so many different
ways.

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:37.530
Why doesn't Bernie just pay more taxes and
send checks to the IRS?

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:42.530
Why does Noam Chomsky, one of the greatest
critics of some of the inequalities in our

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:46.969
economic system, have a trust or some other
mechanism?

00:00:46.969 --> 00:00:47.969
I believe it is.

00:00:47.969 --> 00:00:52.579
So he can transfer his mutual funds, which
include ownership of oil companies to his

00:00:52.579 --> 00:00:57.440
kids while paying as little tax as possible
or whatever the case may be.

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:02.949
We've really got to desegregate this stuff
and and think through in a bit of more critical

00:01:02.949 --> 00:01:05.810
way what we're really asking here.

00:01:05.810 --> 00:01:09.940
Let's take first let's take some examples
first.

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:13.160
If you believe taxes should be higher, why
don't you just send in more money?

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:14.160
That's not policy.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:15.160
OK.

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:16.160
That's not policy.

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:23.250
The idea that just the people who believe
taxes should be higher, sending in more money

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:28.400
is how you resolve a problem with government
tax revenue or fairness or whatever the case

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.360
may be is a joke.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:37.110
And in fact, if everybody isn't do it doing
it, there is really no reason why one person

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:39.240
would do it, because it wouldn't make a difference.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:42.620
And this is why a lot of these things need
to be done collectively.

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:46.420
The groups that like to say just leave this
stuff to charity.

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:47.890
We don't need social safety nets.

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:49.030
We can just leave it to charity.

00:01:49.030 --> 00:01:51.030
Well, maybe, but that's not policy.

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:54.890
Maybe people are more generous versus less
generous one year to the next.

00:01:54.890 --> 00:02:00.340
You can't fix problems in society predictably
with that policy.

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:04.400
So, you know, here in Massachusetts, you have
I think there's this option.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:07.030
You have to pay a higher income tax rate.

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:11.640
I think the income tax rate here is five point
five percent and you can pay like five point

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:12.830
eight if you want.

00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:15.140
I always put no.

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:19.950
And in fact, I actually don't even think the
state income tax needs to be higher.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:23.140
I think where we need more in higher tax brackets
are federally.

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:25.120
But that's a completely different question.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:29.290
Along the same lines, I am a person that exists
in society.

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:32.439
I believe there are many problems with our
economic system.

00:02:32.439 --> 00:02:36.510
But does that mean that what I need to do
is put my money under a mattress where its

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:40.640
purchasing power is diminished by inflation
every single year?

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:42.049
What would that serve?

00:02:42.049 --> 00:02:48.120
Other than to unnecessarily impoverish myself
by keeping money under a mattress?

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:54.120
I believe, for example, that capital gains
should be taxed at or as ordinary income.

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:59.890
Does that mean that when I file my taxes and
I only pay 15 percent on capital gains, I'm

00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:01.400
going to say, hey, you know what?

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:03.159
Let me just send the IRS more money.

00:03:03.159 --> 00:03:04.620
No, that's not policy.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:06.760
There is no hypocrisy.

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:13.920
As long as you are not, you know, advocating
for nonviolence and being a violent person.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:14.920
Right.

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:18.469
I mean, that we can find these types of hypocrisies
that would be different.

00:03:18.469 --> 00:03:24.569
But recognizing that we exist in a certain
financial system, we are people.

00:03:24.569 --> 00:03:27.569
We have a desire for well-being and whatever
else.

00:03:27.569 --> 00:03:34.239
And we are going to play by the rules that
are there while explaining that at a societal

00:03:34.239 --> 00:03:38.499
level, we would be better off if the rules
were changed is not hypocritical.

00:03:38.499 --> 00:03:46.769
Adding And the example of Noam Chomsky having
a trust to I forget the exact response he

00:03:46.769 --> 00:03:48.590
had when he was called out on this.

00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:53.379
Some reporters said, you know, you talk about
inheritance taxes and this that, but you invest

00:03:53.379 --> 00:03:59.180
in mutual funds that hold pieces of oil companies
and also have a trust to give money to your

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:00.180
kids.

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:05.170
Chomsky's reaction was what I should I should
be a popper or I don't remember exactly what

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:06.170
the response was.

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:13.109
But the point is, these are not societal questions
that the individual is making.

00:04:13.109 --> 00:04:14.849
And, of course, you should live your values.

00:04:14.849 --> 00:04:24.610
And if you individually say for me, I would
rather lose my money than have a retirement

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:30.480
possibility that includes owning mutual funds,
then do it, then go ahead and do it.

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:36.890
But to say anybody who thinks oil companies
are bad but owns mutual funds is somehow a

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:38.600
bad person.

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:43.070
Come on, guys, who even has time to go around
making those arguments.

00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:47.570
Let's just work on improving the systems we
have in fixing the problems that we have.

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:51.660
Rather than trying to find these gotcha questions
of people who, you know, have been made have

00:04:51.660 --> 00:05:27.620
made very clear what their values are and
how they believe society should

00:05:27.620 --> 00:06:07.770
be organized.

